window.WIKI_FILES.push({file:"help-contents.md",mtime:1795028966,hash:"8b19243900b8731f369c64783f49204cbb6069779b1fc1ad08a2d00c704380f9",text:`---
title: Help:Contents
categories: [Help]
---

This page explains how the wiki works and how to add to it. For every piece of special syntax, see the [[Help:Formatting|formatting guide]].

## How the wiki is put together

Everything lives in one folder that you can open, copy or upload anywhere:

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| \`index.html\` | The wiki itself. Open it in any browser. |
| \`pages/\` | One Markdown (\`.md\`) file per page. Subfolders are allowed. |
| \`pages/_bundle.js\` | All pages packed into one file. Made by \`build.command\`; never edit it by hand. |
| \`images/\` | Pictures used by pages. |
| \`config.js\` | Site name, tagline, logo, main page and footer. |
| \`build.command\` | Rebuilds \`pages/_bundle.js\` after you change pages. |
| \`assets/\` | The wiki's engine, styles and logo. |

:::important Why there is a build step
Browsers do not let a page opened straight from your disk read other files, so \`index.html\` cannot load the \`.md\` files directly. \`build.command\` packs them into \`pages/_bundle.js\`, which the browser *is* allowed to load. No server and no internet connection are needed.
:::

## Adding or editing a page

1. Create a file in \`pages/\`, for example \`pages/dukkha.md\`.
2. Start it with a header giving the title and categories:
   \`\`\`
   ---
   title: Dukkha
   categories: [Core teachings]
   ---
   \`\`\`
3. Write the article in Markdown below the header.
4. Double-click \`build.command\` (on a Mac). It opens Terminal, rebuilds the bundle and says how many pages it packed.
5. Reload the wiki in your browser.

The file name does not matter to readers; the \`title\` is what links point to. If you leave out \`title\`, the file name is used, with dashes turned into spaces.

:::tip First time on a Mac
If macOS will not open \`build.command\`, right-click it and choose **Open**, or run \`bash build.command\` in Terminal from the site folder.
:::

## Page header options

| Option | Example | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| \`title\` | \`title: Four Noble Truths\` | The page's name, used by links and shown at the top. |
| \`categories\` | \`categories: [Texts, Suttas]\` | Lists the page in those categories. |
| \`summary\` | \`summary: A short description.\` | Used in search suggestions and link previews. Otherwise the first paragraph is used. |
| \`image\` | \`image: wheel.jpg\` | Picture for search suggestions and previews. Otherwise the first infobox image is used. |
| \`redirect\` | \`redirect: Noble Eightfold Path\` | Sends readers to another page. |
| \`toc\` | \`toc: false\` | Hides the contents list. Use \`toc: true\` to force it on short pages. |
| \`displaytitle\` | \`displaytitle: *Dhammapada*\` | Shows a formatted title instead of the plain one. |
| \`updated\` | \`updated: 2026-11-18\` | Overrides the "last edited" date taken from the file. |
| \`ai\` | \`ai: false\` | Hides the "Contains AI-generated content" label. Articles show it unless this is set. |

## Special pages

- [[Special:AllPages]] lists every page.
- [[Special:Categories]] lists every category.
- [[Special:RecentChanges]] lists pages by when their file was last saved.
- [[Special:Random]] opens a random article.
- Every page has **What links here** and **View source** in the sidebar.

Press {{kbd|/}} anywhere to jump to the search box.

## Putting it online

The folder is a complete static website. Upload the whole folder (including \`pages/_bundle.js\`) to any static host and it will work as it does on your computer.
`});
window.WIKI_FILES.push({file:"help-contribute.md",mtime:1795028289,hash:"eb25dabf26ec93696293d1a607b01513ee5e685b51e1f894212ffc06cddd51fd",text:`---
title: Help:Contribute
categories: [Help]
---

This page explains how to contribute and edit contents on this wiki.

## How contribution works

DhammaDB is purposly a closed access wiki. We have done this to prevent misinformation. Although creating content is not possible for users, we have made a expection for editing content. Users may join our Discord server and make a ticket with the **Page ID** and the contents you want to change. Please follow the specified format in the template below. All other formats will not be accepted.

:::important Template for Edit Request
\`Page ID: (Located at the bottom of every page, this is *not* the page name in the page url)\`\\
\`Section: (The section you want to edit)\`\\
\`Draft: (The section rewritten with your changes)\`
:::
`});
window.WIKI_FILES.push({file:"help-formatting.md",mtime:1795008006,hash:"7ff95851ae7ae8b56dda2bb8fadf227bf3e42891217e54c949c21e22fdda1de7",text:`---
title: Help:Formatting
categories: [Help]
---

Pages are written in standard Markdown, plus a few additions that a wiki needs. Each section below shows the syntax and then the result.

## Ordinary Markdown

\`\`\`
**bold**, *italic*, \`code\`, [a website](https://example.org)

- bullet list
1. numbered list

> a block quotation

| Column | Column |
|---|---|
| cell | cell |
\`\`\`

Headings made with \`##\` and \`###\` appear in the contents list automatically. Use \`##\` for main sections; the page title is already the top heading. Tables become sortable when they have three or more rows.

## Links between pages

\`\`\`
[[Four Noble Truths]]
[[Four Noble Truths|the truths]]
[[Four Noble Truths#Cessation]]
[[:Category:Core teachings|]]
[[Tipiṭaka]]s
[[A page that does not exist]]
\`\`\`

Result: [[Four Noble Truths]], [[Four Noble Truths|the truths]], [[Four Noble Truths#Cessation]], [[:Category:Core teachings|]], [[Tipiṭaka]]s, [[A page that does not exist]].

- Text after \`|\` is shown instead of the title.
- \`#Section\` links to a heading on that page.
- An empty \`|\` hides the prefix, so \`[[:Category:Core teachings|]]\` shows just "Core teachings".
- Letters straight after the link become part of it.
- Links to missing pages are shown in red. Clicking one explains how to create the page.

## Categories

Add categories in the page header with \`categories: [Texts, Suttas]\`, or anywhere in the text with \`[[Category:Texts]]\` (this shows nothing where you write it). To *link* to a category instead, start with a colon: \`[[:Category:Texts]]\`.

A category page lists its pages automatically. To add a description, create a page titled \`Category:Texts\`.

## Infobox

The summary box on the right of an article. Each line is \`Label: value\`. A line starting with \`##\` makes a heading row, and \`image:\` with an optional \`caption:\` adds a picture. A bare file name like \`wheel.jpg\` is looked for in the \`images\` folder.

\`\`\`
:::infobox Four Noble Truths
image: dhammacakka.svg
caption: The Dhamma wheel
Pāli: {{term|cattāri ariyasaccāni}}
First taught: [[Dhammacakkappavattana Sutta]]
## Related
Path: [[Noble Eightfold Path]]
:::
\`\`\`

:::infobox Four Noble Truths
image: dhammacakka.svg
caption: The Dhamma wheel
Pāli: {{term|cattāri ariyasaccāni}}
First taught: [[Dhammacakkappavattana Sutta]]
## Related
Path: [[Noble Eightfold Path]]
:::

Put the infobox near the top of the page, before the first paragraph, so the text flows around it.

{{clear}}

## References

Use numbered footnotes, or write the reference inline with \`{{ref|...}}\`. A **References** section is added at the end of the page automatically (before any navigation box). To place it yourself, write \`{{reflist}}\` on its own line.

\`\`\`
Craving is the origin of suffering.[^sn5611]
The first disciple was Koṇḍañña.{{ref|Vinaya, Mahāvagga 1.}}
This needs a source.{{cn}}

[^sn5611]: Saṃyutta Nikāya 56.11.
\`\`\`

Result: Craving is the origin of suffering.[^sn5611] The first disciple was Koṇḍañña.{{ref|Vinaya, Mahāvagga 1.}} This needs a source.{{cn}}

[^sn5611]: Saṃyutta Nikāya 56.11.

{{reflist}}

Using the same footnote name twice reuses its number.

## Hatnotes

Short italic notes at the top of an article or section, pointing readers elsewhere.

\`\`\`
{{main|Dukkha}}
{{see also|Sīla|Samādhi|Paññā}}
{{further|Tipiṭaka}}

:::hatnote
For the discourse, see [[Dhammacakkappavattana Sutta]].
:::
\`\`\`

{{main|Dukkha}}
{{see also|Sīla|Samādhi|Paññā}}
{{further|Tipiṭaka}}

:::hatnote
For the discourse, see [[Dhammacakkappavattana Sutta]].
:::

## Callouts and notices

\`\`\`
:::note
A neutral note.
:::

:::tip Study tip
A helpful suggestion, with a custom title.
:::

:::warning
Something to be careful about.
:::

:::important
Something readers must not miss.
:::

:::notice
A banner for the top of a page, such as "This article is incomplete."
:::
\`\`\`

:::note
A neutral note.
:::

:::tip Study tip
A helpful suggestion, with a custom title.
:::

:::warning
Something to be careful about.
:::

:::important
Something readers must not miss.
:::

:::notice
A banner for the top of a page, such as "This article is incomplete."
:::

## Quotations

\`\`\`
:::quote Dhammapada, verse 1
Mind precedes all things; mind is their chief; they are mind-made.
:::
\`\`\`

:::quote Dhammapada, verse 1
Mind precedes all things; mind is their chief; they are mind-made.
:::

## Pictures

A framed picture with a caption. Give \`left\`, \`right\`, \`center\` or \`none\`, and optionally a width.

\`\`\`
:::figure right 180
dhammacakka.svg
The Dhamma wheel, with eight spokes for the [[Noble Eightfold Path]].
:::
\`\`\`

:::figure right 180
dhammacakka.svg
The Dhamma wheel, with eight spokes for the [[Noble Eightfold Path]].
:::

A gallery shows several pictures in a grid, one per line as \`file | caption\`:

\`\`\`
:::gallery Symbols
dhammacakka.svg | The Dhamma wheel
dhammacakka.svg | Another copy
:::
\`\`\`

:::gallery Symbols
dhammacakka.svg | The Dhamma wheel
dhammacakka.svg | Another copy
:::

Ordinary Markdown images also work: \`![alt text](dhammacakka.svg)\`.

## Navigation box

A box at the foot of related articles. Each line is \`Group: item | item | item\` (spaces around the \`|\` matter).

\`\`\`
:::navbox Core teachings
Truths: [[Four Noble Truths]] | [[Dukkha]] | [[Nibbāna]]
Texts: [[Tipiṭaka]] | [[Dhammacakkappavattana Sutta]]
:::
\`\`\`

:::navbox Core teachings
Truths: [[Four Noble Truths]] | [[Dukkha]] | [[Nibbāna]]
Texts: [[Tipiṭaka]] | [[Dhammacakkappavattana Sutta]]
:::

## Layout blocks

\`\`\`
:::columns 3
- one
- two
- three
- four
- five
- six
:::

:::collapse Show the Pāli
Pāli text that starts hidden.
:::

:::aside Quick facts
A small box floated to the right.
:::
\`\`\`

:::columns 3
- one
- two
- three
- four
- five
- six
:::

:::collapse Show the Pāli
Pāli text that starts hidden.
:::

\`:::grid 2\` with \`:::box Title\` blocks inside it builds panels like the ones on the [[Main Page]]. Blocks can be nested: close each one with its own \`:::\` line.

## Inline templates

| Write | Result | Use |
|---|---|---|
| \`{{lang|Pāli|dhamma}}\` | {{lang|Pāli|dhamma}} | Name a word's language |
| \`{{term|dukkha|suffering}}\` | {{term|dukkha|suffering}} | A foreign term with a gloss |
| \`{{abbr|SN|Saṃyutta Nikāya}}\` | {{abbr|SN|Saṃyutta Nikāya}} | Abbreviation with a hover title |
| \`{{small|text}}\` | {{small|text}} | Smaller text |
| \`{{mark|text}}\` | {{mark|text}} | Highlighted text |
| \`{{badge|New}}\` | {{badge|New}} | A small label |
| \`{{kbd|Ctrl}}\` | {{kbd|Ctrl}} | A key |
| \`{{nowrap|SN 56.11}}\` | {{nowrap|SN 56.11}} | Keep text on one line |
| \`{{cn}}\` | {{cn}} | Citation needed |
| \`{{pagecount}}\` | {{pagecount}} | Number of articles |
| \`{{sitename}}\` | {{sitename}} | The site name from \`config.js\` |

## Lists of pages

These go on a line of their own:

\`\`\`
{{pages in|Core teachings}}
{{recent|5}}
\`\`\`

{{pages in|Core teachings}}

The first lists every page in a category; the second lists the most recently edited pages.

## Redirects

A page whose header contains \`redirect: Other title\` and nothing else sends readers to that page. For example, [[Eightfold Path]] goes to [[Noble Eightfold Path]].
`});
